Z||000009||Fierowrecker||08-26-2001||11:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B> I know it is a joke, but I don't get it...<P>What am I missing?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Go to the parts store and compaire part numbers from a Fiero and a shovit...<BR>Most are identical for suspention parts...<BR>But that is nothing new with any auto maker, the models look different, but the pieces are the same...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pontiaddict||08-27-2001||01:13 AM||||The only parts that are the same are the spindles and the upper control arms. Stuff like tie rod ends and ball joints would be too, but some of those are used in lots of applications. I would hardly call that half of a car.<P>Honestly, I don't think it's possible to make a Chevette any worse, I think i've seen the car Roger is talking about too and it wasn't <I>that</I> bad. You're average riced out Civic is worse. At least it uses two complementing colors.||||reg||1
